WEBVTT

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.730
<i>TURN</i>

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.190
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.110
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:06.690
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.110
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.980
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.360
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>toki ga mirai ni susumu to dare ga kimeta no da?</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<b>Who decided that time should move forward towards the future?</b>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>rakuin o kesu inochi ga rekishi o kakinaosu</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>The lives that will erase these brands will rewrite history</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>utsukushii tsurugi wa hito to hito tsunagete</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<b>People are connected by beautiful, double-edged swords</b>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>meguri kuru setsuna sa kanashimi wo aratte</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>Our coming anticipation will wash away our sadness</b>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>anata to no aida ni inochi aru katachi wo</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<b>With you, between us, life is formed</b>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Kono hoshi ni sasageru ai to iu shirushi de</i>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>With the proof called "love" that we offer to this planet</b>

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.580
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.060
<i>I found a hidden tunnel under the altar that was used for the White Doll's ceremony.</i>

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.860
<i>There, I found weapons fit for the mustached mobile suit,</i>

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.150
<i>but they turned out to be unusable.</i>

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.660
<i>Because of this, I couldn't capture that WaDom.</i>

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:44.150
<i>I was... disappointed.</i>

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:52.170
<b>Training to Be a Lady</b>

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.930
You can let me take care of finding new weapons.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.340
You're in charge, then.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.230
So, can you repair it?

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.150
- I'm not sure.
- What do you mean?

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.360
What? At least say you'll try your best...

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.690
But I need some of the spare parts to repair the other machines.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.660
I can't waste parts.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.160
The real problem is that thing.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.160
So far, we've only found one of them.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.750
You mean the cavern under the shrine didn't have any more of them?

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.150
The sands blew into the tunnel and closed it up again.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.620
I'll go wake Loran up.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.290
He needs to help us move these.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.500
Wait!

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.680
How long were you planning on sleeping for, Loran?!

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.640
Milady!

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.640
- <i>Sochie was praising you.</i>
- Huh?

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.140
She said the Heim's chauffeur is reliable when he puts his mind into it.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.940
- Right?
- l never said that!

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.640
You did too!

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.650
Hey, now that they declared a ceasefire,

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.730
should we really spoil that by fighting again?

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:03.740
Isn't this a great chance for us to get some more mechanical dolls?

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.950
Do you think that's the reason behind this ceasefire?

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:10.100
It seems Lord Guin's factories have begun to manufacture components for mechanical dolls as well.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.250
<i>- No way!</i>
- It's true!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.130
The whole Militia is talking about it.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.630
We still need the White Doll, though,

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.420
so we can't afford to let them capture it.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:23.640
But the delegates for the Earth and moon are negotiating to prevent war from breaking out.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.640
Yeah, but nobody knows how the talks are going.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.430
They may be using their power to force the negotiations to go their way.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.140
I want to meet her.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:32.850
Meet who?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.860
The queen of the moon and her subordinates.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.230
I wonder how I could do that?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.940
That's ridiculous!

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.440
No it's not!

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.110
Then you're just a crazy idiot.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.320
If you really want to meet her so badly,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.950
you may as well just walk the White Doll right into the negotiating area.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.660
Quit being so unreasonable!

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.040
How can I be unreasonable when you're the one making such crazy suggestions?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.630
Oh well, I <i>was</i> wrong about one thing: my opinion of you.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.460
I don't know what's gotten into your head.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.850
I'm only using my judgment to determine the best course of action! What's wrong with that?!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:12.140
Whatever reasons you may have, you shouldn't make excuses.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.350
You're only saying that because you weren't on the front line.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.730
During our investigation today, we discovered that the Terrans

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.820
are excavating their own mobile suits from the Mountain Cycle.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.440
Plus there's more than one like Mountain Cycle with these artifacts in them!

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:37.470
You're suggesting I allow my troops to investigate other mountains that could be like Mountain Cycle?

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.420
If the Earth manages to gain some strength, they'll be far less willing to negotiate.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.510
This is for the sake of avoiding a pointless war.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.550
We cannot go to war.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.640
<i>Ma'am.</i>

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.670
We should hold a party!

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.140
A party?

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:54.440
This way, both sides will have a chance to understand each other, and any pointless battles will be avoided.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:04.080
Keith, are you really going out to vend?

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.490
Good morning.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.150
You didn't need to come here.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:11.160
I'm sorry. If my father hadn't become ill, you never would've...

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.040
Don't worry about it, Miss.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.830
If nobody's coming to the shop, I might as well go out and sell these.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.330
As long as we're in this city, we'll stay in business.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.630
My father said that many of the citizens may have evacuated to the countryside.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.130
<i>We still don't know.</i>

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.040
I'm heading out, Miss.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.510
Anyone want to buy some bread?

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.720
Cheap and delicious bread! Anybody?

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.930
Mama!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.560
I've got delicious bread!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.360
<i>Come, now. When you get to the train, you can eat as much as you want!</i>

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.720
<i>But...!</i>

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.150
The streets are a lot emptier than I expected them to be.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.240
<i>Get outta here, Moonrace!</i>

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.740
Even in a place like this?

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:56.950
You're not goin' any further!

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.630
This land ain't yours, ya bastards!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.660
You tried to crush him to death!

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:09.540
- Damn it!
- Let's have some fun with this guy!

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:13.900
They're shooting!

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.780
Hey, hey! You should've compensated me for this!

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.560
I just baked these this morning.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.640
<i>Hey!</i>

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.350
I didn't do anything.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.650
Those guys just ruined my bread.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.680
<i>Is that bread any good?</i>

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.440
Is it any good?

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:27.940
See for yourself.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:33.800
When you newcomers ask the landowners here for something, you should use a more polite tone.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.830
This is delicious!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:39.040
No wonder everybody wants to come to Earth.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.540
I can't just change the way I talk so easily, though...

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.540
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.050
If you brought this bread to our army, it would sell like crazy.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.170
Everyone would buy it.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.170
You really think so?!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.260
It's delicious. I'll buy all the bread you have here.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.510
- All of it?!
- Yeah, it's great.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.840
Thank you very much, sir!

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:01.190
If we don't restart the negotiations, there's no way we can resolve this matter.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:06.730
I'll send my troops to Nocis City. They'll help you chase those aggressors away!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.940
If we were to attack them now, our chances of winning are one in a thousand!

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.740
A letter from Dianna Soriel.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.440
From Dianna?

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:19.040
She takes us for fools.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.120
It says she hopes to hold a friendship party with us.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.330
A party?!

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:31.930
Is it really alright to send our forces to such an unknown location?

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:36.140
They'll be far away from the mountains where the mechanical dolls are being found, but closer to Nocis city.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.050
We'll get two birds with one stone.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.730
Was that what you dug out yesterday?

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.240
When we saw it, we knew the one thing that Loran used was a weapon...

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.860
But we're not so sure about that one.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.820
No, This one is a weapon too.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.660
I'll need to talk to Loran about it.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.240
Loran went off to see Lord Guin about something.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.330
- When will he be back?
- No idea.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.330
You don't even know your own servant's schedule?

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:09.050
My servant is now responsible for being the White Doll's pilot too.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.960
I can't always keep track of him.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.440
<i>I've been expecting you, Laura Cehack.</i>

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.560
I heard the people downstairs talking. They're throwing a party?

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:34.450
Lieutenant Harry of the Royal Guard said he wishes to meet the White Doll's pilot.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.820
<i>Lieutenant Harry?</i>

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.830
It's a dance party to promote friendship.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.500
He won't hurt you.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.450
But I can't dance...

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.450
This is an order to you, as a Militia pilot.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.580
I don't have the right clothes.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.630
You won't need to worry about that.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.130
That's why I asked Miss Kihel Heim to accompany you.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.260
Miss Kihel, please take care of him.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.760
Of course, sir. Loran, come with me.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.960
Ma'am.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.350
What an impressive wardrobe...

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.440
Yeah.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.850
Actually, I usually use these for our foreign guests.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.860
But now they'll be meant for Laura.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.190
"Laura"?

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.430
For your mission.

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:22.830
In truth, Lord Guin wants Dianna Counter to be aware that we have a mechanical doll just like theirs.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:26.540
And they just so happen to think its driver is a girl.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.830
But why didn't you refuse his request?

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.340
Didn't you want to?

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:34.670
If we can't find a balance, the Earth would get wiped out in a terrible one sided-battle, right?

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.760
I guess.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.760
So I'll do it.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.640
Then before the party starts,

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:43.140
I'll give you lessons on how to behave like a proper lady.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.930
Lessons, you say?

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.600
The cake should look like this.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.350
Is it a snowman?

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.230
<i>It's the Earth and moon.</i>

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.940
- Earth and the moon...
 - I see it now.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.650
I'd like it to be two meters high.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.530
Two meters?! Can we take this order?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.450
We should have the materials, Boss.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:03.240
This is the down payment. We'll give you the rest when you deliver the cake.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.450
T-Thank you.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:04.950
Take care.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.360
<i>Sorry about the wait.</i>

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:09.540
Should we really take an order for the enemy?

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.840
We really need the money right now.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.460
Thank you, Keith.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.420
It's nothing, Miss.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.960
Anyway, about this two-meter cake...

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.230
Didn't I say you mustn't slouch?

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.430
Go ahead.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:36.650
Does it look weird?

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.940
A bit...

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.360
You think so?

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:47.450
You're the one who put it on, Lady Kihel...!

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:53.600
I like this design more than the one the military gave us.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.120
It's a good design, but... Uh--

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.050
It's too heavy.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.260
You're kidding...

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:05.420
A corset will make your waist look thinner...

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.850
Keith!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.550
One, two, three, four!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:43.640
Now spin around!

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:47.470
Don't turn so sharply! Your partner needs to be able to turn with you!

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.560
Alright, now turn around again!

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.440
Be more gentle with your partner!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.400
You call this a partner?!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.650
A lady doesn't criticize her partner's dancing!

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.610
Okay! One, two, three,

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.850
two, two, three, three, two, three...!

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:20.040
Allow me to welcome you all here.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.840
I can't get any good shots from over here.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.550
It's the Militia's mechanical doll!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.250
The White Doll is here?

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:36.050
So the White Doll's pilot has finally shown herself.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:38.640
I can't let you go any further.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:43.210
<i>Guin Rhineford has come as this beautiful lady's escort.</i>

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.030
<i>But aren't there two ladies?</i>

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.990
<i>The Militia doesn't have any guards here?</i>

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.450
l told you to stay back!

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:51.200
But Laura, the White Doll's pilot, is coming out!

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:58.450
Who knows what'll happen tonight.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:06.590
That's Guin and Kihel, so that must be the White Doll's pilot standing between them.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:09.340
<i>Where have I seen her before?</i>

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:12.050
Wait, is that Loran?!

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.050
It's the Dianna Counter Royal Guard.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.150
Lord Guin, there's Lieutenant Harry.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.530
Should we go greet him?

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:26.360
Loran, you're the pilot. Everyone's watching you.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.120
Make sure you behave properly.

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:35.160
Why hello there, Sir Guin. Could that beauty be the mustached mobile suit's pilot?

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.330
Yes. You may call her Laura.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:41.290
On Earth, even such a girl can pilot a mechanical doll.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.690
Pleased to meet you.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:45.050
Let's save the introductions for later.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.010
Yes, sir.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.180
Well then, it's time for the party.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.260
Shall we go, Laura?

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:50.890
Yes, sir.

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:58.260
The ball's preparations should be ready by now! Get a move on!

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:02.720
I didn't realize how hard this would actually be.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.740
Please help yourself to the Earth's wine.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.950
N-no thanks, I don't drink.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.160
There seems to be little difference between the Terrans and ourselves.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.960
<i>This is the first time we've ever had a party like this.</i>

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:22.130
<i>It looks like the soldiers were right all along.</i>

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.760
It looks like both sides are just standing apart from each other and conversing amongst themselves.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.900
If nobody makes the first move, negotiating will be rather difficult.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:32.250
<i>- Well, at least now we know both sides are indeed human!
- Oh, yes.</i>

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.200
I can't see Her Majesty Dianna!

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.350
<i>Laura!</i>

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:40.930
Laura, keep your mouth shut.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:43.020
But I just...

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.520
Politely.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:47.030
This is the first time I have done such a thing.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.450
Well, this isn't much of a friendship party.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.950
They shouldn't just be watching the other side from afar!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.740
They're all the same.

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:56.290
The people of the Earth are conversing amongst themselves.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.250
Now that you mention it, the moon's people are too.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.750
Milady, why don't you go talk to them?

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.040
To the Moonrace?

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.750
Why should I make the first move?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:08.590
If we don't do something, everyone's just gonna stay in one spot, and no one will form any friendships.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:09.760
You're right.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.760
I'll request that someone invites the other members to dance.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.180
<i>I will.</i>

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.140
You can leave it to me.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.060
Very well. Go ahead.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.020
Ma'am.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:20.440
Put on a waltz, if you would.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:21.980
Yes. Right away, sir.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:25.650
With which one of you may I have this dance?

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.030
He's from Dianna Counter.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:29.400
He seems rather unconventional...

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.660
Milady, aren't they being a bit rude?

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.030
Indeed. Well, get out there.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.950
No way! H-how could I--

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:41.120
We wouldn't want those lessons to be for nothing, now would we?

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:44.840
H-How do you do?

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.550
And you are?

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:49.760
I apologize for my ill manners, Mister Lieutenant.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.800
Take my hand, Miss Laura.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:55.850
I-I would... I would be honored, good Lieutenant.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.260
If I may.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.730
We should go too!

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.060
It's our duty, isn't it?

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.360
May I have this dance?

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.230
It would be my pleasure.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:21.160
Now this is more like a party. The food's already almost gone.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.960
And the final touch will be the cake we prepared for the queen of the moon.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.710
Hey, baker! Is the cake ready yet?

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.800
It's all done, but we don't have the stand yet.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.260
Well why not?

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.550
The Militia was supposed to have brought it here already.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.140
You! Go hunt them down!

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.050
Okay.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.430
Isn't that it?

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:39.850
Sorry we're late!

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.350
This is the cake stand you ordered.

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.940
Oh, thank you! I was worried!

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.760
Alright! Let's hurry!

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.440
Her Majesty Dianna...

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.360
- Miss Laura.
 - Yes?

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.450
Where did you find that mobile suit of yours?

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.200
I stumbled upon it on the mountainside.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:02.890
So that means that the Militia has only recently been able to acquire mobile suits, does it not?

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:08.250
While I did stumble upon it accidentally, it wasn't long before we were able to find even more.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.290
What are your thoughts on that?

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.340
Ah.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.630
<i>Additionally,</i>

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.630
<i>it seems there are many more mountains with mobile suits within them.</i>

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:19.720
It would be risky to assume your side possesses the strength to overtake us by force.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.850
Is that what you truly feel?

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.310
It is.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:29.860
I'm terribly sorry to have to interrupt you two,

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:34.080
but I would like to introduce Miss Laura to Her Majesty Dianna. Is that alright?

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:35.240
Go ahead.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.240
To see Her Majesty Dianna?

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:39.030
Miss Laura, if you don't mind, I would like to see you again later.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.120
It would be my pleasure.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:56.550
Your Majesty Dianna Soriel,

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.640
This is the pilot of the White Doll, widely admired by the Militia.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.260
Her name is Laura Rola.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.560
She's quite the beautiful lady.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.730
Pleased to meet you, Laura Rola.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:09.650
The pleasure is mine. Your presence warms my heart,

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.730
Your Excellency Dianna Soriel.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:12.940
Queen Dianna,

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:13.650
Yes?

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:17.360
Now that you are here on Earth, why is the war still continuing?

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.950
Young lady! This is not the time nor place for such things!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.530
Laura! Don't be rude!

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:25.450
Queen Dianna, have you only come to Earth to wage a war?!

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:30.040
You at least could have introduced yourself first, Laura Rola.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.660
O-Of course, Your Majesty.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:36.190
War is the last thing any of us here wish for.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:38.130
Then, if possible,

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:41.010
you intend to do whatever you can to ensure the Earth and Moon coexist peacefully?

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:42.760
Of course.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:46.980
While the two of us may be on opposing sides, I believe that we both share this desire.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.060
Lets work together for each other's benefit.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:50.060
R-Right!

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:56.530
Mr. Guin, there is never reason for those we treasure most to feel unnerved.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:59.030
Would you like to restart the negotiations?

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.230
Of course.

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:07.860
- It's the Earth and moon together!
- I wonder who made it?

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:11.250
The cake of friendship.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.130
Oh! How impressive!

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.750
Your Majesty Dianna, please step forward.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.090
If you would as well, Sir Guin.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.510
<i>Queen Dianna and Lord Guin...</i>

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:29.580
Now, if you two would place the roses into the other's territory as a symbol of friendship.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:34.350
Let us share this cake together as a symbol of coexistence between the Earth and moon!

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.520
Don't mi--

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.030
You bastards!

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:41.290
Don't move!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.990
Dianna!

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.990
If Dianna never came...

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.580
This never would've happened!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.510
You bastards!

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:50.790
Outside?!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.120
- He's the one!
- Right!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.830
Guards! Catch those traitors!

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:58.610
Damn you!

00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:00.260
- Laura!
- Hold it!

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.630
- Are you hurt, Your Majesty?
 - I was fortunate...

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:03.720
<i>Your Majesty Dianna...</i>

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:06.930
We must first prepare a room for Queen Dianna.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.060
But we--

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:10.990
Do you not realize what just happened?

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:13.940
There's obviously no way we can continue the negotiations here.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.400
We... can't?

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:22.360
What the hell is going on, Miss Laura?!

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.740
- They're after Miss Dianna!
- What?!

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:26.730
Miss Rola?!

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.160
Is she going after them in that mobile suit?

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:30.860
<i>Over there!</i>

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.030
<i>Are you trying to catch them?!</i>

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:40.330
Why would you people...?!

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:44.960
One of them got away!

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:50.390
I can't do movements that complex!

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:52.130
They got away?!

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:54.850
Why couldn't you hold onto them?!

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:56.350
Do you want them to get away?!

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:59.320
If I grabbed them any tighter I would have killed them, Lieutenant...!

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.360
Is that the best you can do as a pilot?!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.940
What... is this?

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.200
What?

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.780
It's a portable breathing device.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.320
A breathing device!?

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.740
Were they... Moonrace?!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.530
The assassins used a portable breathing device...

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:24.260
They escaped, but...

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:27.550
It looked to me that they were Militia soldiers.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.850
They were probably acting independently.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:32.890
In that case, we'll root out the responsible party.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:37.850
Furthermore, we hope you will better control the Militia to prevent similar situations from occurring in the future.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:40.210
Do I make myself clear?

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:42.570
You mean you still wish to reopen the negotiations?!

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.650
Fortunately, Her Majesty Dianna was not injured.

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.500
Her feelings on reopening negotiations have not changed.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:49.940
Excuse me.

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:54.160
What were you trying to accomplish?

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.460
What do you mean by that?

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:58.750
You were the one behind this, weren't you?

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:01.420
I'm not clever enough to pull that off.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.760
This problem is on our end.

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:08.840
Has Her Majesty Dianna realized that?

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.350
I believe she has.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:12.170
Guard her well.

00:22:12.170 --> 00:22:13.770
I shall.

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:15.730
<i>I never mentioned it to Laura,</i>

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:19.310
<i>but Miss Kihel truly is the spitting image of Her Majesty Dianna.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:44.060
<i>While I never expected to make friends with a family that returned from the moon,</i>

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:47.640
<i>poor Mr. Kuwen doesn't even have the milk to feed his baby.</i>

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:51.740
<i>As Dianna Counter doesn't seem to care about the civilians,</i>

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:54.500
<i>we began our search for milk.</i>

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:57.580
<i>Lady Sochie even came with us this time!</i>

00:23:59.100 --> 00:24:01.910
<i>Next time, on </i> Turn-A Gundam,

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:03.420
<i>Laura's Cow</i>

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.880
The wind cannot provide us with milk.

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Laura's Cow</b>
